2026-10-23T19:55:00Z  ROOT     Three defects, each necessary: (1) macdeployqt copies libbrotlidec as a dependency of a Qt binary and cannot resolve brotlicommon, and the copied brotlidec keeps LC_RPATH @loader_path/../lib, which inside the bundle names Contents/lib -- absent; (2) STAGE=deploy runs BEFORE macdeployqt, so its closure never includes anything macdeployqt adds; (3) STAGE=verify inspected only the executable's own load commands, so a hole one level down was invisible to the gate that exists to catch exactly this.
2026-10-23T19:55:00Z  CHANGE   cmake/TargetSetup.cmake: new STAGE=fill between macdeployqt and verify. _bundle_machos() enumerates the executable, Contents/Frameworks/*.dylib and each framework's versioned binary (never the Current symlink); _rpaths_of() reads LC_RPATH with @loader_path/@executable_path expanded. For every @rpath dep that does not resolve in the bundle: resolve via the referrer's rpaths then /usr/local/lib, /opt/local/lib, /opt/homebrew/lib; copy with mode 755 and an @rpath/<soname> id; rewrite the reference if the soname differs; repeat until a pass changes nothing (hard error after 9). A framework reference is a hard error rather than a one-file copy.
2026-10-23T19:55:00Z  CHANGE   STAGE=verify now walks every bundle Mach-O (same enumeration) instead of the executable alone, and reports "<macho> -> <dep> (absolute|no such file in the bundle)".
2026-10-23T19:55:00Z  VERIFY   Regenerated build/chadvis-deploy-dylibs.cmake, then ran STAGE=verify against the artifact that had shipped green: it failed with exactly "libbrotlidec.1.dylib -> @rpath/libbrotlicommon.1.dylib (no such file in the bundle)" -- the new gate catches the old hole.
2026-10-23T19:56:00Z  VERIFY   Ran STAGE=fill on the same bundle: "filled libbrotlicommon.1.2.0.dylib (from /usr/local/Cellar/brotli/1.2.0_1/lib/libbrotlicommon.1.2.0.dylib)". Re-verified: "Bundle verified". Re-signed ad-hoc and the app printed its banner, so the fix is proven on the real artifact and not only in the script's own logic.
2026-10-23T20:25:00Z  DEFECT   The first draft of STAGE=fill named the copy after the SOURCE's realpath basename, so a bundle that already carried the library looked like "two different libraries want libbrotlicommon.1.2.0.dylib" and the Release build stopped at deploy. Found by running it, not by reading it. Fixed by naming the copy after the REFERENCE (_rel), which is also the name dyld will look for, so no rewrite is needed in the common case; the change flags now move only on a real copy or rewrite, or the pass loop would never converge.
